# Cloning an Existing GitHub Repository Using SSH

## 1. Add Your SSH Key to GitHub (if not already added)

1. Open **GitHub**.
2. Go to **Settings** → **SSH and GPG Keys**.
3. Click **New SSH Key**.
4. Paste your public SSH key (`id_rsa.pub`) and save it.

---


## 2. Get the Repository SSH Link

1. Open the repository on GitHub.
2. Click the **Code** button.
3. Select **SSH**.
4. Copy the SSH URL.

Example:
git@github.com:username/repository-name.git


---


## 3. Clone the Repository

Open **Command Prompt** and run:


cd Downloads
git clone <paste-the-ssh-url>


Example:
cd Downloads
git clone git@github.com:arunyogi123/donation_platform.git

---


## 4. Get the Latest Changes

To download the latest updates from GitHub:
git pull origin main

This command fetches and merges the latest changes from the `main` branch into your local repository.
